{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>First interpretation</b><br>Kiss. Without a distinguishing letter it is in the mouth, like ישקני (\"kiss me\"); and with a למ\"ד letter, in the hand or on the shoulder or on the cheek, like אשקה נא (\"let me kiss\") (to my father and to my mother), and וישק יעקב לרחל (\"and Jacob kissed Rachel\")." "Your dodim. The singular form דודי is found, like הולך לדודי (\"going to my beloved\") (to straight paths), and it is a noun and sometimes an adjective, like HaShem [i.e., like the Tetragrammaton functioning as both noun and epithet], like שירת דודי (\"the song of my beloved\"). And one of the Geonim said it is the saliva beneath the tongue, on account of לכה נרוה דודים (\"come, let us be intoxicated with dodim\")." "<b>Second interpretation</b><br>A girl from outside the city [in the vineyards] saw a shepherd [passing by] and desired him and longed (in her heart), and said: Who would give that he kiss me many times. And as though he heard her, and she said to him thus: For your dodim are better [than wine], (more) may your beloved rejoice than wine; and because of the fragrance of your oils, for your name is like oil that is poured out whose fragrance spreads — therefore maidens love you. (love you)" "<b>Third interpretation</b><br>He said: Knesset Israel, and began from Abraham, who kept the commandments of HaShem. And the kisses were as it says: ושמר משמרתי מצוותי חקותי ותורותי (\"and he kept My charge, My commandments, My statutes, and My teachings\"). And he delighted more in the worship of HaShem (than) wine, and he showed the deeds of his Elohim, and turned souls back to fear of YHWH."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {1 "The comparison להשם is cryptic; translated hyper-literally without resolving Ibn Ezra's compressed analogy between the morphological behavior of דוד and the divine name.", 3 "Reading והחלה as narrative continuation of אמרה כנסת ישראל, understood as the collective beginning its account from Abraham; the feminine singular verb form is retained from the source."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:55.709035888Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}